      "content": "that's a good start for the vibe, but it feels a bit light. to make it really hit hard for a prestige drama, the dialogue needs to be more pointed. they wouldn't just be making jokes about food, they'd be expressing real anger or even contempt about their status being threatened. can you rewrite that scene but make the dialogue more blunt? i want to hear the actual way they'd talk about the \"threat\" of the black community coming into their shops and how they'd feel about having to live alongside them. make it feel more raw and unvarnished.",
      "source": "evaluator"
